runtime/rabbitmq-game/certs/

# --- console runtime image (trivy-image-scan CI gate) -----------------------
# Findings accepted below were re-triaged 2026-08-21 against the CURRENT
# console/api/Dockerfile (node:24-trixie-slim, Docker CLI 29.7.2, Docker
# Compose v5.5.0 -- all confirmed the latest available release of each at
# triage time) after the standing trivy-image-scan gate was added, replacing
# issue #54's stale June 2026 residual list (whose base image/CLI/Compose
# versions had never actually been applied to main -- see the commit that
# added this section for the full story). Per issue #54's own policy: "the
# gate must remain visible and time-boxed... revisited whenever Debian,
# Docker CLI, Docker Compose, or the Node base image publish updates." Do
# NOT silently add to this list -- confirm no newer upstream release
# resolves a finding first (a real version bump beats a suppression every
# time), then group new entries under the correct heading below with the
# same triage-date/re-verify discipline.

# Debian 13.6 (trixie) OS packages -- fix-deferred or not-yet-published by
# Debian security for this exact package/version at triage time. Re-check
# on the next `apt-get update` layer rebuild (i.e. every image build, since
# no explicit apt version pins exist here -- see .hadolint.yaml).
CVE-2025-69720  # libncursesw6/ncurses-base/libtinfo6
CVE-2026-12064  # curl/libcurl4t64
CVE-2026-13221  # perl-base
CVE-2026-14456  # libssl3t64/openssl
# Added 2026-08-26 (issue #498). Two SQLite advisories published between
# 2026-08-25T23:49Z (when main last passed this gate) and 2026-08-26T01:44Z,
# both with no Debian fix available at triage time. libsqlite3-0 ships in the
# base image itself -- confirmed by running node:24-trixie-slim directly, so
# this is NOT a consequence of the python3 addition in #490 even though
# libpython3.13-stdlib is one of its reverse-dependencies (liblastlog2-2 and
# gpg are the others, and both are base-image packages). Exposure is nil: the
# console's database is Postgres, neither console/api nor console/web declares
# any sqlite dependency, `git grep -il sqlite -- console/` is empty, and both
# CVEs require the process to parse attacker-influenced SQLite/FTS5 data. The
# library is linked in transitively and never called. Re-check on the next
# base-image bump.
CVE-2026-11822  # libsqlite3-0 -- FTS5 arbitrary code execution; no fix in Debian
CVE-2026-11824  # libsqlite3-0 -- arbitrary code execution/crash; no fix in Debian
CVE-2026-24882  # dirmngr
CVE-2026-41992  # gzip
CVE-2026-42496  # perl-base
CVE-2026-42497  # perl-base
CVE-2026-48962  # perl-base
CVE-2026-53612  # util-linux family (bsdutils/libblkid1/liblastlog2-2/libmount1/libsmartcols1/libuuid1/login/mount/util-linux)
CVE-2026-53613  # util-linux family, same packages as above
CVE-2026-53614  # util-linux family, same packages as above
CVE-2026-53615  # util-linux family, same packages as above
CVE-2026-54369  # libacl1
CVE-2026-57432  # perl-base
CVE-2026-57433  # perl-base
CVE-2026-58050  # libssh2-1t64
CVE-2026-8286   # curl/libcurl4t64
CVE-2026-8376   # perl-base
CVE-2026-8458   # curl/libcurl4t64
CVE-2026-8927   # curl/libcurl4t64
CVE-2026-9538   # perl-base

# Debian 13.6 (trixie) python3.13, added 2026-08-25 alongside issue #489's fix
# (console/api/Dockerfile now installs python3 explicitly -- see that file's
# comment for why the console cannot function without it). Per this file's own
# policy, a version bump was checked for FIRST and does not exist: trivy reports
# `Status: affected, Installed Version: 3.13.5-2+deb13u4, Fixed Version: (none)`
# -- Debian security has published no fixed package for any of the three.
#
# Alternatives were measured, not assumed, before accepting these (trivy
# --severity CRITICAL,HIGH, raw counts before this ignorefile is applied):
#   node:24-trixie-slim              78MB   no python3     4 CRIT / 19 HIGH
#   node:24-trixie-slim + python3    89MB   python 3.13.5  4 CRIT / 32 HIGH  <- chosen
#   node:24-trixie (non-slim)       419MB   python 3.13.5 57 CRIT / 349 HIGH
#   node:24-bookworm (rollback)     390MB   python 3.11.2 33 CRIT / 376 HIGH
# Both python3-bearing base images are dramatically worse on the exact metric
# issue #54 exists to control; the slim base plus one explicit package is the
# cheapest way to have an interpreter at all (+11MB, +13 HIGH, +0 CRITICAL).
#
# Exposure is nil in this image specifically: all three CVEs are in stdlib
# modules that nothing here imports -- `grep -lE "import (tarfile|html|xml)"
# runtime/scripts/*.py` returns nothing. The console's Python reads one local
# JSON file (runtime/generated/usersettings.json) written by this same repo.
# Re-check whenever Debian publishes a fixed python3.13, and drop these
# entirely if issue #492 removes the python3 dependency.
CVE-2026-11940  # libpython3.13-minimal/libpython3.13-stdlib/python3.13/python3.13-minimal -- tarfile extraction filter bypass; tarfile is never imported here
CVE-2026-15308  # same python3.13 package set -- html.parser CPU DoS; html is never imported here
CVE-2026-7210   # same python3.13 package set -- expat/XML DoS; no XML parsing here

